  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000122206,
      "SummaryText": "November 2025\nDESCRIPTION OF STATIONARY SOURCE AND REGULATED SUBSTANCES\nThe Rochester terminal is a refined product terminal and storage facility.  It stores and distributes petroleum products such as gasoline and diesel.  A recent project has added butane blending.  Butane will be stored in a single pressurized vessel above threshold quantity, making the blending process at the Rochester terminal a covered process jurisdictional to both OSHA's PSM program and EPA's RMP program.\n\nACCIDENTAL RELEASE PREVENTION AND EMERGENCY RESPONSE POLICIES\nThe Company has a strong commitment to worker and public safety.  Resources have been and will continue to be invested in accident prevention including personnel training, procedure development, design standards and preventative maintenance.\n\nGENERAL ACCIDENTAL RELEASE PREVENTION AND MAINTENANCE PROGRAM\nThe regulated butane storage/blending process is compliant with the fourteen (14) elements of the Process Safety Management/Risk Management Program.  The process controls listed in Section 7.4e include those utilized as safeguards in the PHA.  There could potentially be other process controls used in the process.  The process does not have any trade secrets.  Inspections are conducted and documented to ensure the integrity of the regulated equipment. \n\nFive-Year Accident History\nThe Rochester terminal has not had any accidental releases of the highly hazardous chemical.\n\nEMERGENCY RESPONSE PROGRAM\nThe facility is considered to be a non-responding facility.  \n\nPLANNED CHANGES TO IMPROVE SAFETY\nNo changes are currently planned for the Rochester terminal.  As opportunities for improvements associated with the butane blending system arise, the Company will evaluate the opportunities, assess risks, and mitigate any risks above the accepted criteria limit."
    }
  ]
